SOCIO-ECONOMIC SERVICES

A. LIVELIHOOD TRAINING (NO FEE REQUIRED)
    Requirements:
        Barangay certification confirming that the applicant is a resident of the barangay.
        Accomplished Livelihood Membership Form.
        Steps:
        Proceed to the Barangay Hall and log in to the record book, stating your purpose to the Officer of the Day.
        Inquire with the Livelihood Committee Chairman about the requirements for participating in the livelihood training.
        The Livelihood Committee Chairman will coordinate with the Livelihood President regarding the training schedule and inform the applicant.
        Fees:
        No fee is required for livelihood training.

B. ISSUANCE OF BARANGAY CERTIFICATION FOR SENIOR CITIZENS AND SOLO PARENTS
This certification is a prerequisite for applying for a Senior Citizen ID or Solo Parent ID.
    Requirements:

    1. General Requirement:

        Barangay certification confirming that the applicant is a resident of the barangay.

    2. Senior Citizen Applicants:

        Copy of birth certificate.
        Current Community Tax Certificate (CTC).
        Two (2) copies of 2×2 ID photos.

    3. Solo Parent Applicants:

        Marriage contract and/or birth certificate of dependent(s).
        Current Community Tax Certificate (CTC).
        Two (2) copies of 2×2 ID photos.

C. EDUCATION – DAY CARE SERVICES
    Eligibility Requirement:
        The applicant must be a resident of the barangay and duly registered in the Barangay Census.
        Enrollment Requirements:
        Accomplished enrollment form provided by the Day Care Worker.
        Photocopy of birth certificate.
        Growth Monitoring Card.
    Steps:
        Proceed to the Barangay Hall and inquire with the Education Committee Chairman about the enrollment schedule.
        The Day Care Worker will provide an enrollment form to be completed by the parent or guardian for reservation.
        The parent or guardian must submit the accomplished enrollment form, photocopy of the birth certificate, and Growth Monitoring Card to the Day Care Worker.
        Coordinate with the Day Care Worker regarding the schedule of daycare sessions.

D. DELIVERY OF BASIC SERVICES – NFA ROLLING STORE
    Eligibility Requirements:
        The applicant must be a resident of the barangay and duly registered in the Barangay Census.

    Steps:
        Proceed to the Barangay Hall and coordinate with the Chairman of the Family and Education Committee to make a reservation and arrange the appropriate payment.
        The Committee Chairman will coordinate with the NFA Rolling Store regarding the number of rice sacks (cavans) requested by the residents.
        The NFA Rolling Store will deliver rice to the Barangay for the convenience of residents.
        Additional rice purchases may be made available for residents who were unable to reserve rice due to financial constraints.
        Fees and Payment:
        Payment is required for rice reservations.
        The specific price or amount of payment is not specified in the current knowledge base.